1
00:00:01,105 --> 00:00:02,665
Let me be your roommate, Khobfa.

2
00:00:02,745 --> 00:00:06,425
<i>If you make one shot out of five,</i>
<i>I'll let you be my roommate.</i>

3
00:00:09,785 --> 00:00:10,785
Did it go in?

4
00:00:15,625 --> 00:00:16,825
It did.

5
00:00:16,905 --> 00:00:17,905
Yo, my roommate!

6
00:00:17,985 --> 00:00:20,145
But you have to promise me something.

7
00:00:20,785 --> 00:00:24,385
If anything unlucky happens,
you have to move out right away.

8
00:00:24,985 --> 00:00:25,905
Okay.

9
00:00:29,665 --> 00:00:30,585
-Deal!
-Deal!

10
00:00:31,105 --> 00:00:35,425
My name is Khobfa.

11
00:00:35,505 --> 00:00:39,465
I am eight years old.

12
00:00:40,145 --> 00:00:46,425
I like to eat fried rice,

13
00:00:47,225 --> 00:00:50,305
and I want…

14
00:00:51,625 --> 00:00:57,905
to help my fa…

15
00:01:02,545 --> 00:01:03,585
…ter.

16
00:01:15,265 --> 00:01:16,225
Okay.

17
00:01:16,305 --> 00:01:17,745
It's fine, sweetheart.

18
00:01:17,825 --> 00:01:18,745
"Father."

19
00:01:18,825 --> 00:01:20,705
Try pronouncing it. "Father."

20
00:01:20,785 --> 00:01:21,665
Father.

21
00:01:21,745 --> 00:01:25,665
Okay. Make sure to pronounce it correctly
before helping your father.

22
00:01:25,745 --> 00:01:27,065
Got it, sweetheart?

23
00:01:34,465 --> 00:01:37,385
<i>Keep this in mind, students. We're Thai.</i>

24
00:01:37,465 --> 00:01:40,025
We should be brave to speak English.

25
00:03:10,825 --> 00:03:11,705
Come on.

26
00:03:12,305 --> 00:03:13,705
-Ouch.
-Here. I'll help you.

27
00:03:14,825 --> 00:03:16,785
Man, you're really going all out.

28
00:03:17,385 --> 00:03:18,585
Going all out for what?

29
00:03:19,105 --> 00:03:23,625
Moving in with a tough guy like Khobfa.

30
00:03:24,585 --> 00:03:25,625
What do you mean?

31
00:03:27,065 --> 00:03:29,185
We know what you're trying to do.

32
00:03:30,465 --> 00:03:32,785
You're trying to get back at Krit, right?

33
00:03:32,865 --> 00:03:35,225
Nice one, bro. That's smart.

34
00:03:37,145 --> 00:03:38,745
Actually, I--

35
00:03:38,825 --> 00:03:39,905
It's fine, Rin.

36
00:03:39,985 --> 00:03:42,265
You're still our friend. I'm cool with it.

37
00:03:43,705 --> 00:03:47,225
But if Khobfa finds out about your plan
and does anything bad to you,

38
00:03:47,305 --> 00:03:48,745
tell us right away.

39
00:03:48,825 --> 00:03:51,505
Yeah, Rin. You have to tell us right away.

40
00:03:51,585 --> 00:03:54,305
But this is the right move.
Revenge has to be served.

41
00:03:54,385 --> 00:03:56,065
You're seriously smart.

42
00:03:56,145 --> 00:03:57,665
You're an amazing friend.

43
00:03:58,705 --> 00:04:00,265
-Let's go.
-Let's go.

44
00:04:01,345 --> 00:04:02,985
Yeah. Let's do this.

45
00:04:17,585 --> 00:04:19,425
<i>I'm here. What are you doing?</i>

46
00:04:22,145 --> 00:04:25,705
GIVE ME A SEC. I JUST WOKE UP.

47
00:04:25,785 --> 00:04:29,105
Guys, I feel like
I'm forgetting something.

48
00:04:29,185 --> 00:04:32,145
Should we take a selfie for my story?

49
00:04:32,225 --> 00:04:33,505
-Sure.
-Yeah?

50
00:04:33,585 --> 00:04:36,305
Sending our friend into a guy's room
for the first time!

51
00:04:36,385 --> 00:04:38,185
What do you mean by that?

52
00:04:38,265 --> 00:04:40,745
Stop complaining and take the picture.

53
00:04:40,825 --> 00:04:42,065
Ready?

54
00:04:42,145 --> 00:04:44,785
Three, two, one.

55
00:04:52,945 --> 00:04:54,185
Well…

56
00:04:55,545 --> 00:04:59,585
This is Ohm, and this is Jinnie.

57
00:05:00,185 --> 00:05:01,705
My friends.

58
00:05:01,785 --> 00:05:03,105
Yeah.

59
00:05:04,745 --> 00:05:06,305
Can I ask you something?

60
00:05:08,545 --> 00:05:10,825
Why did your landlord
ask for the house back?

61
00:05:16,025 --> 00:05:17,745
-We wrecked it.
-The owner sold the property.

62
00:05:17,825 --> 00:05:18,825
Huh?

63
00:05:18,905 --> 00:05:21,985
-The owner sold the property.
-We wrecked the house…

64
00:05:22,585 --> 00:05:25,745
-Well… The pipes broke, right?
-Well…

65
00:05:25,825 --> 00:05:29,105
Well, the landlord's renovating the place.

66
00:05:29,185 --> 00:05:31,385
-Yeah. Right.
-Right. Renovating.

67
00:05:31,465 --> 00:05:33,945
-And property prices have gone up too.
-Right.

68
00:05:34,025 --> 00:05:35,585
So we had to hurry and move out.

69
00:05:35,665 --> 00:05:37,105
-It was exhausting.
-Yeah.

70
00:05:37,185 --> 00:05:39,305
I'm still not done packing.

71
00:05:39,385 --> 00:05:40,785
Me neither.

72
00:05:40,865 --> 00:05:43,065
All right, good luck. See you later.

73
00:05:43,145 --> 00:05:44,145
See you later.

74
00:05:58,905 --> 00:06:00,225
Should I bring my stuff in now?

75
00:06:08,145 --> 00:06:11,305
So, what are your roommate rules?

76
00:06:11,385 --> 00:06:12,585
I can handle anything.

77
00:06:17,545 --> 00:06:20,585
Don't move any
of my personal belongings, ever.

78
00:06:23,505 --> 00:06:25,705
Yeah, sure.

79
00:06:26,305 --> 00:06:27,385
Same goes for my stuff.

80
00:06:28,345 --> 00:06:29,225
Don't touch them.

81
00:06:31,745 --> 00:06:32,825
Fine.

82
00:06:33,985 --> 00:06:35,105
What's next?

83
00:06:36,585 --> 00:06:38,185
You're studying fine arts, right?

84
00:06:38,265 --> 00:06:39,265
Yeah.

85
00:06:39,345 --> 00:06:41,385
Don't get paint all over my room.

86
00:06:41,465 --> 00:06:44,585
Easy. What else?

87
00:06:44,665 --> 00:06:50,265
I'm a clean freak.
Don't make my room dirty. Got it?

88
00:06:59,785 --> 00:07:01,265
Don't make the room dirty. Got it.

89
00:07:01,945 --> 00:07:03,185
Yeah.

90
00:07:03,265 --> 00:07:04,385
The bed is over there.

91
00:07:06,305 --> 00:07:08,065
Wow.

92
00:07:14,305 --> 00:07:17,905
So I sleep in the bed,
and you sleep down there, right?

93
00:07:18,505 --> 00:07:19,745
That's cute.

94
00:07:20,465 --> 00:07:21,305
Wait.

95
00:07:23,705 --> 00:07:25,305
You've got it wrong.

96
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:28,625
You sleep down there. I sleep in the bed.

97
00:07:30,705 --> 00:07:32,225
I think you said that wrong.

98
00:07:32,305 --> 00:07:34,025
Who gets the bed? Say it again.

99
00:07:35,505 --> 00:07:38,225
You sleep down there.

100
00:07:42,825 --> 00:07:43,985
Got it?

101
00:07:46,705 --> 00:07:47,705
Right.

102
00:07:48,825 --> 00:07:50,065
Where's the bathroom?

103
00:08:03,905 --> 00:08:05,065
Hang in there.

104
00:08:05,145 --> 00:08:06,305
I can do this.

105
00:08:08,865 --> 00:08:12,185
Once his birthday comes,
it'll all be over.

106
00:08:27,225 --> 00:08:28,465
Shit!

107
00:08:30,865 --> 00:08:31,865
What happened?

108
00:08:33,904 --> 00:08:37,425
Who told you
to leave your boxers lying here, idiot?

109
00:08:58,185 --> 00:09:01,065
I'm giving you one week.
You can stay here--

110
00:09:01,145 --> 00:09:04,065
"But nothing unlucky
can happen because of you."

111
00:09:04,665 --> 00:09:08,025
If anything bad happens to me,
I'm leaving this room right away.

112
00:09:08,625 --> 00:09:11,465
You've said that five times already.
I remember.

113
00:09:12,865 --> 00:09:14,585
I'm keeping my eye on you.

114
00:09:15,425 --> 00:09:17,105
I'm the one keeping an eye on you.

115
00:09:17,185 --> 00:09:18,825
No, I'm keeping my eye on you.

116
00:09:19,865 --> 00:09:21,265
I'm keeping my eye on you.

117
00:09:21,345 --> 00:09:22,665
I'm keeping my eye on you.

118
00:09:22,745 --> 00:09:23,585
Me.

119
00:09:23,665 --> 00:09:25,665
-No, me.
-I'm keeping an eye on you.

120
00:09:25,745 --> 00:09:28,225
-Me.
-I'm the one watching you.

121
00:09:40,585 --> 00:09:44,705
<i>I'm his roommate now. I'll try my best</i>
<i>to stay with him until his birthday.</i>

122
00:09:44,785 --> 00:09:47,025
<i>Then you can stop worrying now.</i>

123
00:09:53,385 --> 00:09:54,345
Khobfa.

124
00:09:58,865 --> 00:10:01,585
Hey. Nothing unlucky
happened to you today, right?

125
00:10:02,505 --> 00:10:03,945
Is that how you say hello?

126
00:10:16,425 --> 00:10:17,945
Stand farther away.

127
00:10:32,465 --> 00:10:33,665
So what's the plan?

128
00:10:34,185 --> 00:10:35,545
We've been waiting forever.

129
00:10:38,905 --> 00:10:39,825
Let's go inside.

130
00:10:55,185 --> 00:10:58,945
You two always arrive together these days.

131
00:11:00,385 --> 00:11:03,705
We're roommates.
Of course we arrive together.

132
00:11:04,225 --> 00:11:05,345
Right?

133
00:11:08,905 --> 00:11:09,825
Yeah.

134
00:11:11,705 --> 00:11:14,665
So I guess we're condo buddies now.

135
00:11:23,945 --> 00:11:25,385
Why are you going this far, Rin?

136
00:11:33,265 --> 00:11:34,145
What do you mean?

137
00:11:34,225 --> 00:11:35,905
All of this.

138
00:11:36,545 --> 00:11:37,945
Why do you have to go this far?

139
00:11:40,025 --> 00:11:41,345
How far is "this far"?

140
00:11:41,425 --> 00:11:42,985
As far as what you did to me?

141
00:11:45,065 --> 00:11:48,225
Seriously, Krit.
You have no right to say that to me.

142
00:11:49,585 --> 00:11:50,825
I'm only asking

143
00:11:52,465 --> 00:11:53,905
because I'm worried about you.

144
00:12:00,665 --> 00:12:02,145
<i>It's over.</i>

145
00:12:02,225 --> 00:12:03,825
<i>No matter what you do,</i>

146
00:12:04,425 --> 00:12:06,265
we're already over.

147
00:12:17,505 --> 00:12:19,265
You said things between you were over,

148
00:12:20,945 --> 00:12:23,345
so make sure they really are.

149
00:12:59,185 --> 00:13:00,945
Just leave me here.

150
00:13:03,385 --> 00:13:04,225
Okay.

151
00:13:05,225 --> 00:13:08,665
Take care of yourself.

152
00:13:09,665 --> 00:13:10,505
Yeah.

153
00:13:24,305 --> 00:13:25,865
TOP 5 FINALISTS

154
00:13:28,305 --> 00:13:31,945
If you're going to do this,
it should be more evenly matched.

155
00:13:34,305 --> 00:13:35,785
What are you talking about?

156
00:13:36,385 --> 00:13:39,385
Look at Khobfa.

157
00:13:40,585 --> 00:13:42,225
I don't think
he can easily compete with Krit.

158
00:13:45,465 --> 00:13:47,825
How do you know Khobfa can't beat Krit?

159
00:13:48,465 --> 00:13:53,585
Just wait and see whether Krit or Khobfa
will be the one who wins.

160
00:13:54,905 --> 00:13:55,905
Fine.

161
00:14:07,945 --> 00:14:09,545
Is your pitching presentation ready?

162
00:14:10,425 --> 00:14:11,665
I'm waiting to coach you.

163
00:14:13,185 --> 00:14:15,745
I just told the professor I'm withdrawing.

164
00:14:17,025 --> 00:14:17,865
What?

165
00:14:19,145 --> 00:14:21,225
Why would you withdraw?

166
00:14:22,625 --> 00:14:24,385
What are you so scared of?

167
00:14:24,465 --> 00:14:26,745
I can help you beat Krit.

168
00:14:28,905 --> 00:14:30,625
Why do I have to beat Krit?

169
00:14:31,385 --> 00:14:35,025
What? Don't you want to beat someone
who looked down on you?

170
00:14:36,625 --> 00:14:38,505
You're always like this.

171
00:14:38,585 --> 00:14:40,745
You just let people look down on you.

172
00:14:44,905 --> 00:14:46,225
You don't know anything.

173
00:14:46,865 --> 00:14:48,185
Can you stay out of it?

174
00:14:59,545 --> 00:15:00,785
Seriously?

175
00:15:00,865 --> 00:15:02,265
Why did Khobfa withdraw?

176
00:15:02,865 --> 00:15:04,105
I'm not sure.

177
00:15:04,865 --> 00:15:06,465
Well, that's good.

178
00:15:07,065 --> 00:15:08,905
Just do your best.

179
00:15:08,985 --> 00:15:11,265
I'm sure you can win
the championship again.

180
00:15:11,345 --> 00:15:14,385
Honestly, I'm still not that confident.

181
00:15:15,465 --> 00:15:19,025
The last time I won,
it was partly because of Rin.

182
00:15:19,625 --> 00:15:23,305
Hey, you can stand on your own now.

183
00:15:23,385 --> 00:15:26,585
You're really good.
Believe in yourself more.

184
00:15:29,145 --> 00:15:32,585
Show Rin that you can do
just fine without him.

185
00:15:33,825 --> 00:15:36,465
If I win,

186
00:15:37,105 --> 00:15:38,225
do I get a reward?

187
00:15:38,985 --> 00:15:41,385
What do you want?

188
00:15:44,025 --> 00:15:45,465
My…

189
00:15:49,945 --> 00:15:52,105
foot or my fist?

190
00:15:52,625 --> 00:15:56,585
Come on, Mochi. That's not very creative.

191
00:15:57,265 --> 00:15:58,305
I'm kidding.

192
00:15:59,225 --> 00:16:01,225
Fine. I'll treat you…

193
00:16:02,345 --> 00:16:04,585
I'll treat you to an omakase.

194
00:16:04,665 --> 00:16:09,865
Oh, really? Wow, thank you so much.

195
00:16:10,465 --> 00:16:14,505
<i>I'm working on it as fast as I can.</i>
<i>Prof. James isn't going to yell at me.</i>

196
00:16:15,185 --> 00:16:17,905
<i>How are you doing?</i>
<i>How's your roommate? Is he okay?</i>

197
00:16:23,905 --> 00:16:25,065
I guess.

198
00:16:26,465 --> 00:16:29,745
I was talking to him just fine,
but then he turned his ass toward me.

199
00:16:36,945 --> 00:16:38,265
Stop playing already.

200
00:16:38,785 --> 00:16:41,345
Why? You can't handle it?

201
00:16:43,585 --> 00:16:47,505
If you can't, go stay somewhere else.
You don't have to be my roommate.

202
00:16:52,105 --> 00:16:53,105
Seriously, you…

203
00:16:54,425 --> 00:16:57,185
Try talking back to other people
the way you do to me.

204
00:17:24,305 --> 00:17:25,424
Khobfa!

205
00:17:58,625 --> 00:17:59,785
<i>You're a jinx.</i>

206
00:17:59,865 --> 00:18:00,785
I'm sorry.

207
00:18:00,865 --> 00:18:03,025
<i>Everyone in this family died</i>
<i>because of you.</i>

208
00:18:03,105 --> 00:18:04,865
<i>Why didn't you die instead, Khobfa?</i>

209
00:18:05,505 --> 00:18:06,945
I didn't do it.

210
00:18:10,865 --> 00:18:12,545
I'm a jinx, aren't I?

211
00:18:12,625 --> 00:18:14,905
I'm the reason Mom and Dad died.

212
00:18:36,625 --> 00:18:41,745
I'm sorry I'm a jinx.

213
00:20:33,465 --> 00:20:34,985
<i>I'm sorry, Dad.</i>

214
00:20:35,665 --> 00:20:37,425
<i>I don't think I can do it.</i>

215
00:22:32,945 --> 00:22:34,185
Why did you mess with my stuff?

216
00:22:38,065 --> 00:22:43,745
If we ignore the grammar
and add a little more sincerity,

217
00:22:44,505 --> 00:22:46,305
I think this is already pretty good,

218
00:22:47,825 --> 00:22:51,465
especially the part inspired by your dad.

219
00:22:55,665 --> 00:22:57,145
You should stay in the competition.

220
00:23:00,065 --> 00:23:01,545
But I'm not good at English.

221
00:23:02,545 --> 00:23:04,625
I got made fun of for it as a kid.

222
00:23:17,545 --> 00:23:19,705
You can always practice a language.

223
00:23:25,025 --> 00:23:26,505
But what's in here…

224
00:23:29,545 --> 00:23:31,505
and in here…

225
00:23:32,545 --> 00:23:35,665
I think they're already amazing.

226
00:23:39,065 --> 00:23:40,665
You don't need to practice them.

227
00:23:40,745 --> 00:23:42,665
Just stay in the competition.

228
00:23:44,745 --> 00:23:47,185
Don't do it for anyone else.

229
00:23:56,705 --> 00:23:58,225
Just go up there

230
00:23:59,185 --> 00:24:03,425
and imagine you're telling your dad
about your project.

231
00:24:15,185 --> 00:24:16,705
Let me help you.

232
00:24:17,305 --> 00:24:21,585
Consider it part of me
being your roommate.

233
00:24:22,385 --> 00:24:23,625
Let me do something for you.

234
00:24:25,905 --> 00:24:28,945
Please? Come on. Please.

235
00:24:33,825 --> 00:24:36,265
Please. I'm begging you.

236
00:24:36,945 --> 00:24:38,425
Please let me help you.

237
00:24:39,625 --> 00:24:42,625
Fine. Okay. Let's do it.

238
00:24:44,105 --> 00:24:45,345
Yay!

239
00:24:48,745 --> 00:24:52,825
I'll help you, so don't worry.
I'm going to train you hard, okay?

240
00:24:52,905 --> 00:24:55,545
I'll turn you into
a top businessman in this country.

241
00:24:56,145 --> 00:24:58,905
I guarantee your pitch will be amazing.

242
00:25:05,385 --> 00:25:09,905
"My project is helping people
to can have a house."

243
00:25:09,985 --> 00:25:12,665
Hey. You can't say "to can."

244
00:25:13,265 --> 00:25:14,945
Then what am I supposed to say?

245
00:25:15,545 --> 00:25:20,025
This part should be,
"helps people own a house."

246
00:25:20,105 --> 00:25:24,025
"And asset owners unlock the hidden value
of what they already have."

247
00:25:24,105 --> 00:25:26,585
"This is not just a smarter way to spend."

248
00:25:26,665 --> 00:25:29,265
"It's a smarter way to live. Thank you."

249
00:25:30,105 --> 00:25:31,265
Was it okay?

250
00:25:31,865 --> 00:25:33,425
I think…

251
00:25:34,785 --> 00:25:35,705
It was okay.

252
00:25:36,985 --> 00:25:37,985
<i>Okay.</i>

253
00:25:38,065 --> 00:25:41,185
"My project is help people own house

254
00:25:41,865 --> 00:25:46,225
because my father, he working very hard,
but still don't have a house."

255
00:25:46,945 --> 00:25:47,785
Wrong.

256
00:25:47,865 --> 00:25:49,545
You just need to smile a little more.

257
00:25:49,625 --> 00:25:52,265
Smile often. You look cute when you smile.

258
00:25:54,585 --> 00:25:59,465
"He works very hard
but still doesn't have a house."

259
00:25:59,545 --> 00:26:00,465
That's better.

260
00:26:00,545 --> 00:26:01,465
Yes!

261
00:26:01,545 --> 00:26:04,465
Now, when you speak,
you have to speak from the heart.

262
00:26:05,025 --> 00:26:07,625
You have to feel it, okay?

263
00:26:08,905 --> 00:26:10,025
<i>How do I smile?</i>

264
00:26:10,625 --> 00:26:13,385
Well, smile like this.

265
00:26:24,265 --> 00:26:25,385
Do I look cute now?

266
00:26:29,825 --> 00:26:31,345
Do you think I can do it?

267
00:26:41,545 --> 00:26:44,945
You really like competitions, don't you?

268
00:26:45,465 --> 00:26:46,985
They're challenging.

269
00:26:47,585 --> 00:26:51,505
And maybe my family
will finally be proud of me.

270
00:27:00,425 --> 00:27:03,945
I believe your family
will be proud of what you do.

271
00:27:07,265 --> 00:27:09,305
Just like I've always been proud of you.

272
00:27:15,025 --> 00:27:18,625
You're proud of me?

273
00:27:21,465 --> 00:27:22,385
I guess.

274
00:27:23,065 --> 00:27:24,385
I don't know.

275
00:27:25,105 --> 00:27:26,785
Well, if you win,

276
00:27:26,865 --> 00:27:29,385
then Rin can stop using Khobfa
to make you jealous.

277
00:27:35,185 --> 00:27:36,265
<i>You're a jinx.</i>

278
00:27:36,345 --> 00:27:37,225
I'm sorry.

279
00:27:37,305 --> 00:27:39,705
<i>Everyone in this family died</i>
<i>because of you.</i>

280
00:27:39,785 --> 00:27:41,985
Stop talking to your grandson like that.

281
00:27:42,065 --> 00:27:44,025
He didn't do anything wrong.

282
00:27:44,105 --> 00:27:46,145
KHUNKAO CHAIPANHA
MAR 6,1980-JAN 12, 2020

283
00:27:46,225 --> 00:27:47,745
Khobfa, sweetheart.

284
00:27:47,825 --> 00:27:49,745
Why didn't you die instead, Khobfa?

285
00:27:49,825 --> 00:27:50,745
Stop it!

286
00:27:50,825 --> 00:27:52,705
I didn't want this to happen.

287
00:27:55,705 --> 00:27:56,705
I'm sorry.

288
00:27:58,745 --> 00:27:59,825
I didn't mean to.

289
00:28:02,225 --> 00:28:03,985
I didn't want any of this to happen.

290
00:28:17,425 --> 00:28:18,545
Here.

291
00:28:25,825 --> 00:28:27,505
You didn't sleep well last night?

292
00:28:28,785 --> 00:28:29,625
Yeah.

293
00:28:30,265 --> 00:28:32,265
I've been having bad dreams lately.

294
00:28:34,385 --> 00:28:35,945
Want me to take you to campus?

295
00:28:38,025 --> 00:28:41,265
No need.
Don't you have an afternoon class?

296
00:28:41,865 --> 00:28:45,625
But how will you get there?
You'll drive when you're this sleepy?

297
00:28:47,505 --> 00:28:48,785
That's my problem.

298
00:29:30,385 --> 00:29:31,665
What happened to Khobfa?

299
00:29:35,145 --> 00:29:37,025
He probably got into trouble again.

300
00:29:37,105 --> 00:29:38,905
When is Ohm getting here?

301
00:29:38,985 --> 00:29:40,705
-We've been waiting forever.
-Yeah.

302
00:29:41,665 --> 00:29:42,825
Rin, Jinnie!

303
00:29:43,465 --> 00:29:45,225
-Look at this.
-Huh?

304
00:29:45,305 --> 00:29:47,065
What the hell did Khobfa do?

305
00:29:47,785 --> 00:29:49,585
Everyone's sharing it.

306
00:29:49,665 --> 00:29:51,985
They're saying that thug
got into another fight.

307
00:29:52,065 --> 00:29:54,385
He looks like
he got into a fight with a dog.

308
00:29:55,065 --> 00:29:56,425
Your roommate…

309
00:29:56,985 --> 00:29:58,545
Be careful around him.

310
00:30:01,785 --> 00:30:02,825
Let me see.

311
00:30:06,705 --> 00:30:07,865
Look at him.

312
00:30:07,945 --> 00:30:11,225
<i>The number you have dialed</i>
<i>cannot be reached at this time.</i>

313
00:30:11,305 --> 00:30:13,305
<i>Please leave your message.</i>

314
00:30:16,945 --> 00:30:18,065
-What?
-Hey!

315
00:30:43,465 --> 00:30:45,025
Where are you, Khobfa?

316
00:30:47,265 --> 00:30:48,745
Are you looking for me?

317
00:30:50,265 --> 00:30:51,465
Khobfa!

318
00:30:55,185 --> 00:30:56,665
What happened to you?

319
00:30:58,465 --> 00:31:00,745
I just fell off my motorbike this morning.

320
00:31:02,105 --> 00:31:04,665
I told you. If you're sleepy, don't drive.

321
00:31:05,785 --> 00:31:09,385
I just didn't get enough sleep.
I only blacked out for a second.

322
00:31:09,465 --> 00:31:11,025
It wasn't because of bad luck.

323
00:31:19,385 --> 00:31:22,105
Can you please stop getting yourself hurt?

324
00:31:36,025 --> 00:31:38,585
<i>What should I do?</i>
<i>His bad luck is starting again.</i>

325
00:31:39,185 --> 00:31:42,105
<i>He's been having nightmares so often</i>
<i>that he doesn't get enough sleep.</i>

326
00:31:42,185 --> 00:31:43,785
<i>Then he rode his motorbike and crashed.</i>

327
00:31:46,025 --> 00:31:47,305
<i>Easy, kid.</i>

328
00:31:47,385 --> 00:31:50,065
<i>Maybe he's not unlucky.</i>
<i>Maybe he's just sleep-deprived.</i>

329
00:31:53,785 --> 00:31:54,665
<i>Exactly.</i>

330
00:31:54,745 --> 00:31:57,905
<i>Nothing beats a good night's sleep</i>
<i>and sweet dreams.</i>

331
00:32:06,225 --> 00:32:07,305
What are you making?

332
00:32:09,785 --> 00:32:12,985
A dreamcatcher.
They're really trendy right now.

333
00:32:13,945 --> 00:32:14,905
What's that?

334
00:32:14,985 --> 00:32:17,545
Self-care is really trendy these days.

335
00:32:17,625 --> 00:32:19,905
If you're going to be healthy,
go all the way,

336
00:32:19,985 --> 00:32:22,665
both when you're awake
and when you're asleep.

337
00:32:22,745 --> 00:32:27,425
Basically, the web catches the bad dreams

338
00:32:27,505 --> 00:32:31,625
and lets the good dreams pass through,
so you can sleep peacefully.

339
00:32:34,145 --> 00:32:35,545
Seriously?

340
00:32:35,625 --> 00:32:36,785
Of course.

341
00:32:37,465 --> 00:32:40,465
Wait, you're wearing one too.

342
00:32:41,065 --> 00:32:42,545
You don't know what it means?

343
00:32:44,265 --> 00:32:48,425
No. My mom gave it to me,
but I never knew what it meant.

344
00:32:57,985 --> 00:33:01,665
<i>Nothing beats a good night's sleep</i>
<i>and sweet dreams.</i>

345
00:33:17,265 --> 00:33:18,185
Ouch.

346
00:33:22,665 --> 00:33:24,185
Why is it so tight?

347
00:33:39,465 --> 00:33:40,305
Ouch.

348
00:34:00,905 --> 00:34:03,265
I hope this helps you, Khobfa.

349
00:34:12,585 --> 00:34:14,705
Hey, what are you doing?

350
00:34:16,465 --> 00:34:20,665
I thought it looked nice, so I was
going to decorate the room with it.

351
00:34:24,985 --> 00:34:28,385
No. If you want to hang that up,
hang it on your side.

352
00:34:29,824 --> 00:34:33,625
Come on. Something like this
looks best by the window.

353
00:34:33,705 --> 00:34:36,105
But this is my side. I don't like it.

354
00:34:37,425 --> 00:34:39,465
Just leave it. You'll like it eventually.

355
00:34:40,505 --> 00:34:42,145
Why are you forcing me?

356
00:34:42,744 --> 00:34:44,225
Did you forget this is my room?

357
00:34:45,185 --> 00:34:46,865
Stop messing with my stuff.

358
00:34:53,545 --> 00:34:56,665
Hey, but this can stop your nightmares.

359
00:35:02,705 --> 00:35:05,545
It's called a dreamcatcher.

360
00:35:07,625 --> 00:35:10,945
You've been having nightmares
and not getting enough sleep.

361
00:35:12,025 --> 00:35:13,545
I just wanted to help you.

362
00:35:19,865 --> 00:35:21,905
I don't want it. I'm fine.

363
00:35:42,985 --> 00:35:45,825
Rin, can we talk?

364
00:35:47,705 --> 00:35:48,705
What is it?

365
00:35:50,025 --> 00:35:53,585
I know I don't have the right
to tell you who you can date.

366
00:35:54,505 --> 00:35:58,145
But if you're going to date someone,
can't you choose someone better?

367
00:36:02,345 --> 00:36:03,585
What do you mean?

368
00:36:07,505 --> 00:36:11,265
Didn't you tell me yourself
to stay away from Khobfa?

369
00:36:11,345 --> 00:36:14,025
So what's this?
You're getting close to him now.

370
00:36:15,545 --> 00:36:18,745
Nobody wants Khobfa.
He's nothing but bad luck.

371
00:36:19,545 --> 00:36:20,385
Krit.

372
00:36:20,985 --> 00:36:22,905
I never thought
you'd be this kind of person.

373
00:36:23,505 --> 00:36:26,185
I don't care
what other people say about Khobfa.

374
00:36:26,745 --> 00:36:30,465
The Khobfa I know
is nothing like what they say.

375
00:37:04,225 --> 00:37:05,105
Here.

376
00:37:05,705 --> 00:37:06,825
I got this for you.

377
00:37:19,065 --> 00:37:22,745
Why are you waiting for me
in front of my faculty?

378
00:37:25,705 --> 00:37:28,185
We're supposed to practice
our presentation today.

379
00:37:36,225 --> 00:37:37,465
Thanks…

380
00:37:42,065 --> 00:37:43,825
for standing up for me like that.

381
00:37:44,425 --> 00:37:45,585
You heard that?

382
00:37:50,905 --> 00:37:52,945
People just say whatever they want.

383
00:37:53,025 --> 00:37:55,145
I felt uncomfortable
hearing them talk like that.

384
00:38:00,825 --> 00:38:02,025
I'm sorry.

385
00:38:02,865 --> 00:38:05,545
I might've made you
uncomfortable yesterday too.

386
00:38:08,145 --> 00:38:10,105
Maybe I really am what they say I am.

387
00:38:11,185 --> 00:38:12,665
I don't think so.

388
00:38:18,545 --> 00:38:19,385
Come on.

389
00:38:19,465 --> 00:38:22,185
Let's practice the presentation
and prove them wrong.

390
00:38:41,465 --> 00:38:44,025
Okay. Today, we're practicing
without a script.

391
00:38:44,105 --> 00:38:46,705
It'll be like
you're actually onstage. Okay?

392
00:38:47,345 --> 00:38:51,745
Then imagine
I'm a top businessman in the country,

393
00:38:51,825 --> 00:38:54,185
looking for a new business to invest in.

394
00:38:54,265 --> 00:38:56,425
Whenever you're ready, the floor is yours.

395
00:39:06,905 --> 00:39:09,665
My… name is…

396
00:39:17,505 --> 00:39:20,825
<i>Keep this in mind, students. We're Thai.</i>

397
00:39:20,905 --> 00:39:23,025
We should be brave to speak English.

398
00:39:24,825 --> 00:39:26,345
My name…

399
00:39:28,545 --> 00:39:29,625
What's wrong?

400
00:39:30,425 --> 00:39:31,865
I'm not used to this!

401
00:39:36,225 --> 00:39:38,345
I had to present in front of the class
when I was a kid.

402
00:39:38,425 --> 00:39:41,785
I said something wrong,
and my teacher laughed at me.

403
00:39:42,865 --> 00:39:45,865
I can't do it.
I can't speak in front of people!

404
00:39:52,705 --> 00:39:55,825
So what did that teacher look like?

405
00:40:30,305 --> 00:40:31,905
What was her name?

406
00:40:32,785 --> 00:40:34,105
Teacher Maratee.

407
00:40:35,265 --> 00:40:36,745
Teacher Maratee.

408
00:40:36,825 --> 00:40:40,105
With all due respect,
what kind of teacher are you?

409
00:40:40,705 --> 00:40:43,145
Just because a kid can't speak English
in front of the class,

410
00:40:43,225 --> 00:40:44,705
that doesn't mean he's stupid.

411
00:40:45,225 --> 00:40:48,505
Wait. You're the one teaching him, right?

412
00:40:48,585 --> 00:40:51,945
So maybe the problem is
you didn't teach him properly.

413
00:40:52,025 --> 00:40:53,625
And another thing.

414
00:40:53,705 --> 00:40:56,785
Making a kid stand there
while everyone laughs at them isn't right.

415
00:40:58,065 --> 00:41:00,145
Come on. Your turn.

416
00:41:00,665 --> 00:41:01,745
Huh?

417
00:41:03,025 --> 00:41:04,185
Scold her.

418
00:41:09,185 --> 00:41:10,105
Yeah.

419
00:41:11,025 --> 00:41:12,585
You shouldn't do that.

420
00:41:15,345 --> 00:41:17,305
Come on, harsher than that.

421
00:41:27,785 --> 00:41:28,905
Yeah!

422
00:41:29,505 --> 00:41:31,345
You know some kids
aren't good at this subject,

423
00:41:31,425 --> 00:41:33,065
but they're still trying their best.

424
00:41:33,145 --> 00:41:34,345
What kind of teacher are you?

425
00:41:34,425 --> 00:41:37,345
Is making fun of your own student
hilarious to you or something?

426
00:41:47,305 --> 00:41:48,585
Thanks.

427
00:41:49,665 --> 00:41:51,305
I'll do my best.

428
00:41:52,625 --> 00:41:54,225
I promise I won't let you down.

429
00:41:59,905 --> 00:42:01,505
Don't do it for me.

430
00:42:02,145 --> 00:42:04,145
Don't worry about what anyone else says.

431
00:42:04,905 --> 00:42:06,985
Just tell them what you want to tell them.

432
00:42:40,305 --> 00:42:44,305
This platform lets people rent items
instead of buying them,

433
00:42:44,385 --> 00:42:48,425
so they only pay
for what they actually use.

434
00:42:49,825 --> 00:42:50,985
At the same time,

435
00:42:51,065 --> 00:42:54,945
the owners can earn from items
they already have but rarely use.

436
00:42:56,145 --> 00:42:58,185
We simply connect both sides

437
00:42:58,785 --> 00:43:01,105
without holding inventory.

438
00:43:01,865 --> 00:43:03,825
Students,
if you haven't finished your work,

439
00:43:03,905 --> 00:43:05,305
you're not going anywhere.

440
00:43:05,385 --> 00:43:07,305
It's just a simple landscape drawing.

441
00:43:07,865 --> 00:43:10,145
-Ohm, hurry up.
-Okay.

442
00:43:10,225 --> 00:43:14,425
So it turns unused assets
into real assets.

443
00:43:18,825 --> 00:43:21,025
This is not just a smarter way to spend.

444
00:43:23,225 --> 00:43:25,505
This is a smarter way to live.

445
00:43:27,505 --> 00:43:28,385
Thank you.

446
00:43:35,385 --> 00:43:36,265
<i>Look at Krit.</i>

447
00:43:36,865 --> 00:43:38,505
He nailed the presentation.

448
00:43:40,265 --> 00:43:41,305
<i>Incredible!</i>

449
00:43:41,385 --> 00:43:43,545
Prof, can you just
finish the class already?

450
00:43:53,305 --> 00:43:54,625
You did amazing.

451
00:43:55,305 --> 00:44:02,305
All right. Next is the second contestant,
Mr. Watchiravit Kaoiam.

452
00:44:06,345 --> 00:44:07,625
You did very well today.

453
00:44:07,705 --> 00:44:09,985
Leave your work with your friend.
Collect and submit them.

454
00:44:10,065 --> 00:44:12,745
-See you, everyone. Thank you very much.
-Thank you. Goodbye.

455
00:44:12,825 --> 00:44:13,865
Collect the assignments.

456
00:44:13,945 --> 00:44:16,465
Hey, can you pack my stuff for me?
I've got to go.

457
00:44:16,545 --> 00:44:17,865
-Go ahead.
-Hurry up.

458
00:44:18,465 --> 00:44:20,145
Sending my support to Khobfa!

459
00:44:20,225 --> 00:44:21,945
Hurry up, dude!

460
00:44:32,945 --> 00:44:33,825
Khobfa.

461
00:44:36,865 --> 00:44:38,665
-What are you doing here?
-Excuse me.

462
00:44:38,745 --> 00:44:40,465
-Be careful!
-Khobfa!

463
00:44:53,305 --> 00:44:54,385
You almost got hurt.

464
00:44:55,025 --> 00:44:56,065
Thanks.

465
00:44:57,185 --> 00:44:58,265
Are you ready?

466
00:45:07,265 --> 00:45:08,145
I'm ready.

467
00:45:09,305 --> 00:45:10,505
Let's go.

468
00:45:11,145 --> 00:45:11,985
Let's go.

469
00:45:15,545 --> 00:45:16,505
Oops!

470
00:45:19,025 --> 00:45:20,065
I'm sorry.

471
00:45:26,065 --> 00:45:27,665
-Shit!
-Shit!

472
00:45:44,705 --> 00:45:45,745
Take off your shirt.

473
00:45:45,825 --> 00:45:46,785
Huh?

474
00:45:46,865 --> 00:45:48,305
Just wear mine for now.

475
00:45:48,985 --> 00:45:49,905
Hurry.

476
00:46:02,825 --> 00:46:04,025
Let's switch.

477
00:46:09,465 --> 00:46:10,385
Thanks.

478
00:46:10,905 --> 00:46:14,185
When you're with me, the unlucky things
that happen seem so small.

479
00:46:20,865 --> 00:46:21,785
Come here.

480
00:46:36,265 --> 00:46:37,305
All done.

481
00:46:39,025 --> 00:46:42,785
Hey, can I leave my dad's pen with you?

482
00:46:52,025 --> 00:46:52,945
Of course.

483
00:46:55,305 --> 00:46:57,465
I'll take the best care
of your dad for you.

484
00:46:57,545 --> 00:46:58,625
I promise.

485
00:47:01,065 --> 00:47:01,945
Thanks.

486
00:47:03,865 --> 00:47:04,705
Hey, wait.

487
00:47:09,865 --> 00:47:10,785
And this…

488
00:47:21,545 --> 00:47:22,945
for good luck.

489
00:47:27,985 --> 00:47:30,625
Thanks. I'm going now.

490
00:47:33,105 --> 00:47:34,385
Good luck.

491
00:47:39,665 --> 00:47:41,785
Let's go see how amazing your son is, Dad.

492
00:47:51,665 --> 00:47:54,025
-Am I on time?
-Yeah, but…

493
00:47:55,545 --> 00:47:57,105
What happened to your shirt?

494
00:47:58,865 --> 00:48:00,305
Forget about it.

495
00:48:00,385 --> 00:48:01,865
Is that your shirt?

496
00:48:02,425 --> 00:48:03,545
Is that yours?

497
00:48:03,625 --> 00:48:06,905
-Don't worry about it. Just watch him.
-Our final contestant is…

498
00:48:06,985 --> 00:48:08,745
Mr. Khobfa Chaipanha!

499
00:48:30,545 --> 00:48:31,705
You can do it.

500
00:48:35,025 --> 00:48:38,465
This project didn't start with numbers,

501
00:48:39,585 --> 00:48:43,185
not with profit,
not with a business model.

502
00:48:45,345 --> 00:48:47,985
But it started with my dad,

503
00:48:51,945 --> 00:48:55,465
an ordinary man
who has worked his whole life

504
00:48:57,425 --> 00:49:01,425
and yet still doesn't have
a home of his own.

505
00:49:02,185 --> 00:49:04,105
Not because he didn't try,

506
00:49:04,705 --> 00:49:08,505
but because he never had
the same opportunities.

507
00:49:09,105 --> 00:49:12,905
So I created HomeStep,

508
00:49:14,585 --> 00:49:18,185
a platform that doesn't only sell homes,

509
00:49:18,265 --> 00:49:23,945
but also helps ordinary people
move closer to owning their homes,

510
00:49:24,025 --> 00:49:25,745
step by step.

511
00:49:25,825 --> 00:49:28,105
<i>Don't do it for anyone else.</i>

512
00:49:28,185 --> 00:49:29,545
<i>Just go up there</i>

513
00:49:29,625 --> 00:49:34,145
and imagine you're telling your dad
about your project.

514
00:49:34,745 --> 00:49:35,785
<i>You're a jinx.</i>

515
00:49:35,865 --> 00:49:37,785
<i>Everyone in this family died</i>
<i>because of you.</i>

516
00:49:37,865 --> 00:49:39,545
<i>Why didn't you die instead, Khobfa?</i>

517
00:49:39,625 --> 00:49:41,825
<i>Don't let anyone hurt you, okay?</i>

518
00:49:42,825 --> 00:49:44,545
<i>Don't worry about what anyone else says.</i>

519
00:49:45,505 --> 00:49:47,585
Just tell them what you want to tell them.

520
00:49:48,185 --> 00:49:49,785
From financial guidance

521
00:49:50,905 --> 00:49:52,225
to building credit

522
00:49:52,825 --> 00:49:56,545
and to finding a home
they can truly afford.

523
00:49:57,425 --> 00:49:58,625
Because in the end,

524
00:49:59,225 --> 00:50:02,265
a home is not just a place to live.

525
00:50:02,345 --> 00:50:04,345
It is stability.

526
00:50:05,065 --> 00:50:09,465
It is the dignity that everyone deserves.

527
00:50:10,265 --> 00:50:11,185
Thank you.

528
00:50:22,265 --> 00:50:24,665
<i>And now, I have the final results</i>
<i>in my hands.</i>

529
00:50:25,265 --> 00:50:28,225
This year's winner is…

530
00:50:43,945 --> 00:50:45,785
Mr. Kritchaphat Iamchaisree.

531
00:50:52,105 --> 00:50:53,185
We have something special this year.

532
00:50:53,265 --> 00:50:55,425
Another contestant received
the exact same score.

533
00:50:59,945 --> 00:51:01,385
And that person is…

534
00:51:10,905 --> 00:51:12,585
Mr. Khobfa Chaipanha!

535
00:51:20,065 --> 00:51:24,265
THE GRAND PRIZE
PITCHING BUSINESS MODEL 2026

536
00:51:29,945 --> 00:51:31,905
THE GRAND PRIZE
PITCHING BUSINESS MODEL 2026

537
00:51:31,985 --> 00:51:34,905
See that, Dad? Your son did amazing!

538
00:51:49,185 --> 00:51:50,105
Congrats.

539
00:51:53,785 --> 00:51:56,225
Thanks. You too.

540
00:52:00,025 --> 00:52:01,865
You usually prefer being alone.

541
00:52:03,505 --> 00:52:05,305
Why did you agree
to let Rin be your roommate?

542
00:52:06,265 --> 00:52:07,345
Why don't you ask Rin?

543
00:52:14,025 --> 00:52:15,065
Does Rin like you?

544
00:52:25,025 --> 00:52:26,145
I don't know.

545
00:52:27,745 --> 00:52:28,985
What about you?

546
00:52:32,305 --> 00:52:33,465
Do you like Rin?

547
00:53:09,865 --> 00:53:12,025
-Yeah! Cheers!
-Yeah!

548
00:53:12,105 --> 00:53:14,305
Come on, everyone! Let's drink to Khobfa!

549
00:53:14,385 --> 00:53:15,385
Drink, drink.

550
00:53:19,065 --> 00:53:21,265
Hey, Khobfa.
You're number one to me today.

551
00:53:21,345 --> 00:53:25,585
I know you're cochampions,
but I'm giving you first place today.

552
00:53:25,665 --> 00:53:26,745
Seriously.

553
00:53:26,825 --> 00:53:31,225
When they announced the results,
Mochi and Krit looked so shocked.

554
00:53:31,305 --> 00:53:33,425
-I saw it too.
-Come on, how did they look?

555
00:53:33,505 --> 00:53:34,785
Like this.

556
00:53:35,945 --> 00:53:37,025
Totally shocked.

557
00:53:37,105 --> 00:53:39,625
-Shit, you look just like…
-Like what? Watch your mouth.

558
00:53:39,705 --> 00:53:41,585
-Like Krit and Mochi!
-Yeah.

559
00:53:41,665 --> 00:53:44,345
Yeah! They really looked like this.
They were completely stunned.

560
00:53:44,425 --> 00:53:46,505
Come on, make a shocked face.

561
00:53:46,585 --> 00:53:48,785
-Yeah, yeah.
-He just moved his nostrils.

562
00:53:50,305 --> 00:53:52,665
Your turn. Do it!

563
00:53:53,345 --> 00:53:54,225
-Hey!
-Hey!

564
00:53:54,305 --> 00:53:56,385
-What's that?
-That's hilarious.

565
00:53:57,465 --> 00:53:59,905
-Come on. Cheers!
-Cheers!

566
00:54:02,505 --> 00:54:04,705
You look so dumb.

567
00:54:04,785 --> 00:54:06,065
Then you do it.

568
00:54:08,665 --> 00:54:10,585
Was your mouth really like that?

569
00:54:12,025 --> 00:54:13,425
They were totally stunned!

570
00:54:13,505 --> 00:54:15,265
-Yeah.
-Really?

571
00:54:22,145 --> 00:54:24,145
I told you to drink slowly.

572
00:54:24,905 --> 00:54:27,465
I just wanted to celebrate with you.

573
00:54:28,065 --> 00:54:29,905
Congratulations.

574
00:54:41,305 --> 00:54:42,545
Hold on tight.

575
00:54:42,625 --> 00:54:44,025
It'll keep you safe.

576
00:54:45,065 --> 00:54:46,025
Okay.

577
00:54:46,625 --> 00:54:50,145
I'll hold on to you tight,
so you won't run into any more bad luck.

578
00:55:04,505 --> 00:55:09,345
<i>A presto amora!</i>

579
00:55:10,545 --> 00:55:12,105
Go to sleep. Go on.

580
00:55:19,105 --> 00:55:20,465
What are you even saying?

581
00:55:21,865 --> 00:55:24,745
You don't have to be afraid
of nightmares tonight.

582
00:55:25,665 --> 00:55:27,585
Go. Sleep properly.

583
00:55:46,465 --> 00:55:48,025
You're lucky, you know.

584
00:55:49,065 --> 00:55:51,185
You can fall asleep anywhere.

585
00:55:57,505 --> 00:55:58,545
<i>What about you?</i>

586
00:55:59,785 --> 00:56:00,945
Do you like Rin?

587
00:56:22,625 --> 00:56:24,265
Remember what I told you?

588
00:56:25,585 --> 00:56:27,225
Whenever you're with me,

589
00:56:28,025 --> 00:56:30,785
all the unlucky things that happen
seem so small.

590
00:56:33,665 --> 00:56:35,465
I really mean that.

591
00:56:45,505 --> 00:56:47,745
You've got Rin with you tonight, kid.

592
00:56:48,545 --> 00:56:49,825
Sweet dreams.

593
00:57:00,105 --> 00:57:02,745
<i>A presto amora!</i>

594
00:57:02,825 --> 00:57:04,145
Hey!

595
00:57:30,305 --> 00:57:35,585
Our activity this semester
is a nature camp.

596
00:57:35,665 --> 00:57:37,505
This camp is amazing.

597
00:57:37,585 --> 00:57:40,625
<i>There's even a legend about a tree</i>
<i>that can prove true love.</i>

598
00:57:40,705 --> 00:57:45,105
<i>Guys, I think Khobfa's acting weird today.</i>

599
00:57:45,185 --> 00:57:46,905
<i>I think I really like you.</i>

600
00:57:46,985 --> 00:57:48,225
Can I hit on you?

601
00:57:49,465 --> 00:57:50,465
<i>Thank you so much.</i>

602
00:57:50,545 --> 00:57:53,625
<i>If it weren't for you, I probably</i>
<i>wouldn't have tried anything new.</i>

603
00:57:53,705 --> 00:57:55,505
<i>Rin isn't here, Khobfa.</i>

604
00:57:55,585 --> 00:57:57,425
<i>Rin, don't let anything happen to you.</i>

605
00:57:58,785 --> 00:57:59,745
Rin!

